
Week 2 - Day 1
Topic: CSS Box Model and Display Properties

1. What is the CSS Box Model?

The CSS Box Model explains how every HTML element is displayed as a box on a webpage. It consists of content, padding, border and margin. It helps us control the size and spacing of elements.

2. Difference between margin and padding?

Margin is the space outside an element's border, whereas padding is the space between the content and the border.

3. Difference between block and inline?

Block elements start on a new line and usually take the full available width. Inline elements do not start on a new line and take only the space they need.

4. Why do we use box-sizing: border-box?

We use box-sizing: border-box because it includes padding and border in the total width and height of an element. It makes it easier to manage the size of cards and other elements.
